# What's New (automatic)

When you finish Hub work that ships (commit to main), update
`src/shared/whatsNew.ts` in the **same commit** when the change qualifies.
Do not wait for Grant to ask.

## Put an entry when

- The change affects **all directors/teachers** (shared chrome, rolls UX,
  Today, schedule alerts, auth shell, shared director tools).
- The change affects **what students/families see** on the public site
  (home, calendar, ensembles, event cards, lookup, documents, PWA shell).

Use `audience: 'staff' | 'public' | 'both'` to match who should see the
banner. Prefer one entry per ship day; merge related bullets. Set
`expires` ~2 weeks out. Bump `id` if re-showing a revised tip.

## Do NOT put an entry when

- Ensemble-specific content Grant (or any director) enters in the app:
  repertoire, concerts details, announcements they write, roster edits,
  seating, documents uploaded for one program.
- Allowlist / access admin: adding a teacher, changing a role, directors
  collection seed.
- Pure refactors, tests, docs, CI, or scripts with no user-visible change.
- One-off Firestore data fixes that are not a product/UX change (unless
  the fix itself changes how the site is read, e.g. opening-week schedule
  for everyone).

## Launch day hold (2026-08-13 only)

On **2026-08-13**, do **not** add or keep any entry with
`audience: 'public'` or `audience: 'both'`. Public home stays clean so
students go straight to the main info. Staff-only tips are fine.
From **2026-08-14** onward, public / both entries may ship again as usual.

## Entry shape

```ts
{
  id: 'YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug',
  date: 'YYYY-MM-DD',
  title: 'Plain, student-friendly headline',
  audience: 'both', // or staff / public
  expires: 'YYYY-MM-DD', // ~14 days later
  bullets: [
    'What changed, in plain language.',
    'Where to look, if useful.',
  ],
}
```

Replace or prune expired/stale entries when adding new ones so the banner
does not pile up. Empty `WHATS_NEW` is fine when nothing qualifies.
